;; The award subsystem, frozen, end to end. the design record: fund before declare, one admin
;; operation per transaction.
;; 🔴 the design record: a round needs a SEALED RECORD DATE, and sealing one on a FROZEN module is
;; itself part of the freeze claim — `schedule-snapshot` is ADMIN-gated and
;; `advance-snapshot` WRITES, so if either died at the freeze the award subsystem below
;; could never run again on that chain. §6 asserts both directly; this is the end-to-end.
;; ---- the design record (a later change): A ROUND NEEDS A SEALED RECORD DATE ----------------------
;; Schedule one clear of the 12h runway (2 x MIN-RETRACT-LEAD), let it land, seal it.
;; The seal runs with NO KEYS on purpose: `advance-snapshot` is permissionless, and a
;; chain with no activity must still be sealable by anyone.
(begin-tx "the design record: name the record date")
(env-keys ["admin-key"])
(n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.schedule-snapshot
  (add-time (at 'block-time (chain-data)) 43202))
(commit-tx)
(env-chain-data
  { "chain-id": (at 'chain-id (chain-data))
, "block-time": (add-time (at 'block-time (chain-data)) 43203) })
(begin-tx "the design record: seal it")
(env-keys [])
(n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.advance-snapshot)
(commit-tx)

(begin-tx "2 tokens declare-round works frozen")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-08T00:00:02Z") })
(env-keys ["admin-key"])
(expect "declare-round works frozen" "round declared"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.declare-round "FRZ-R1" 0.01 (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z")))
;; 🔴 get-round's exists:TRUE BRANCH — the `with-read`, the only path in it that can abort and
;; the entire reason the function was added. §2's three get-round assertions all hit
;; exists:FALSE, and the comment there claimed "BOTH BRANCHES are exercised, deliberately".
;; THAT CLAIM WAS FALSE (an internal review completeness critic, F-D): no test in the repo reached
;; the read, while the enumeration gate and the MANDATORY-step gate both passed on it. This is
;; the only place in this suite where a round actually exists, so it is where the branch lives.
(expect "get-round: a DECLARED round reads back FROZEN with exists:true"
  true (at 'exists (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-round 1)))
(expect "get-round: and its real rate, not the zero default"
  0.01 (at 'rate (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-round 1)))
(commit-tx)

