(begin-tx "2 tokens release-tranche works frozen (permissionless, the design record)")
;; a later amendment (a later change): release-tranche is FOUNDER-ONLY now, so the frozen exercise moved
;; from "liquidity" to setup.repl's founder row. Past the founder cliff (T+365d) it pays.
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2027-06-02T00:00:00Z") })
(expect "release-tranche pays out frozen" true
  (> (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.release-tranche
       "founder:k:f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0") 0.0))
(commit-tx)

;; a later amendment (a later change): DISBURSEMENT WORKS FROZEN — the whole point of building it
;; pre-freeze. The treasury tranche is past its cliff at this block-time, "alice" is a real
;; holder created in the seed above, and the payment lands. A disbursement that stopped
;; working at freeze would strand 70% of supply in the reserves FOREVER, which is the
;; a finding defect shape this suite exists to catch.
(begin-tx "2 tokens disburse-tranche works frozen (ADMIN, a later amendment)")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2027-06-02T00:00:00Z") })
;; 🔴 a later change: `DISBURSE` is `@managed`, so the frozen path is exercised the way it will
;; actually be signed — a clist entry naming the exact tranche, target and budget. `env-keys`
;; alone now fails with "Managed capability not installed", which would make this suite report
;; a freeze defect that does not exist. THE FREEZE PROPERTY IS UNCHANGED: the meter is part of
;; the capability, not of GOVERNANCE, so it behaves identically frozen and unfrozen — and the
;; budget still BINDS after the freeze, which §G below pins by name.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "admin-key", "caps": [(n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.DISBURSE "treasury" "alice" 10.0)] }])
(expect "disburse-tranche pays out frozen" 10.0
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.disburse-tranche
    "treasury" "alice" 10.0))
(expect "the disbursed tokens really landed, frozen" true
  (>= (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-balance "alice") 10.0))
;; 🔴 a later change: AND THE BUDGET STILL BINDS WHEN FROZEN. The budget above was exactly 10.0 and it
;; is now spent, so a second call on the SAME frozen module must be refused by the manager —
;; not by the calendar, which still has the rest of the treasury vested. Without this the
;; enumeration would record that `disburse-tranche` survives the freeze while saying nothing
;; about whether the LIMIT does, and a meter that quietly stopped metering after the freeze is
;; unfixable by construction.
(expect-failure "the DISBURSE budget still binds on a FROZEN module"
  "DISBURSE exceeded: 10.0 requested of 0.0 managed"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.disburse-tranche
    "treasury" "alice" 10.0))
(commit-tx)

(begin-tx "2 tokens debit is still correctly UNREACHABLE from tx code when frozen")
;; env-data restored deliberately: the credit negative below reads a keyset, and without it the
;; call aborts on `read-keyset failure` BEFORE reaching `credit` — the assertion would then be
;; green while testing nothing. The 3-arg form caught exactly that here, which is the whole
;; argument for a later change's conversion of all 82 negatives.
(env-data { "alice": { "keys": ["alice-key"], "pred": "keys-all" } })
;; Not a freeze effect — the same refusal holds unfrozen (an internal review a finding). Asserted so the
;; enumeration covers `debit` with the reason it cannot be called directly, rather than
;; omitting it and leaving a reader to wonder.
(expect-failure "debit refuses without DEBIT in scope, frozen exactly as unfrozen"
  "not granted"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.debit "alice" 1.0))
(expect-failure "credit refuses without CREDIT in scope, frozen exactly as unfrozen"
  "not granted"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.credit "alice" (read-keyset 'alice) 1.0))
(rollback-tx)

;; ===========================================================================
;; §3 — SPT-launch: EVERY PUBLIC FUNCTION, FROZEN.
;; THIS MODULE HAD ZERO FROZEN-STATE COVERAGE BEFORE a later change. It is the reason this item
;; exists, and the sale is the module a buyer touches.
;;
;; NOT-RUNNABLE in this scenario:
;; init one-shot, already ran in the seed. §5 proves the frozen module
;; still REACHES its own one-shot guard, i.e. the refusal is
;; "already initialized" and not a freeze effect.
;; launch-reserve-guard /
;; sales-proceeds-guard defconst-bound at load; exercised implicitly by every reserve
;; and proceeds spend below (the accounts ARE their principals)
;; enforce-not-initialized reached only through init
;; ===========================================================================
(begin-tx "3 launch READS all answer frozen")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
(expect "get-price works frozen" 0.5 (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.get-price))
(expect "is-active works frozen" true (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.is-active))
(expect "reserve-account works frozen" n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.LAUNCH-RESERVE-ACCOUNT
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.reserve-account))
(expect "proceeds-account works frozen" n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.SALES-PROCEEDS-ACCOUNT
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.proceeds-account))
;; the design record part 2: enforce-price takes the floor as a PARAMETER now (init runs before the
;; config row exists, so it cannot read one). Passing the live floor is the frozen-path
;; equivalent of what set-price does.
;; the design record (a later change): the address-only half of the beneficiary chain, exercised frozen. It is a
;; pure string check with no authority, so the freeze cannot reach it — asserted anyway, because
;; "it obviously still works" is the reasoning an internal review a finding defeated.
(expect "enforce-beneficiary-address works frozen" true
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.enforce-beneficiary-address
    "k:f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0"))
(expect-failure "and it still REFUSES a non-principal frozen"
  "beneficiary must be a k:/w: principal"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.enforce-beneficiary-address "vanity-name"))
(expect "enforce-price works frozen" true
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.enforce-price 0.5
    (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.get-min-price)))
(commit-tx)

(begin-tx "3 launch buy works frozen — THE SALE STILL SELLS")
;; The single most important assertion in this file for SPT-launch: a buyer can still
;; buy from a frozen module. It spans BOTH frozen modules — coin payment in, then
;; SPT.transfer-create out of the reserve under Pattern E.
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
(env-data { "carol": { "keys": ["carol-key"], "pred": "keys-all" } })
(env-sigs [{ "key": "admin-key", "caps": [(coin.TRANSFER "sender00" "carol" 250.0)] }])
(coin.transfer-create "sender00" "carol" (read-keyset 'carol) 250.0)
(commit-tx)
(begin-tx "3 launch the purchase itself")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
(env-sigs [{ "key": "carol-key", "caps": [(coin.TRANSFER "carol" (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.proceeds-account) 250.0)] }])
(expect "buy works frozen" "tokens purchased"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.buy "carol" (read-keyset 'carol) 500.0))
(expect "carol holds the SPT she bought from a frozen sale" 500.0
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-balance "carol"))
(commit-tx)

(begin-tx "3 launch pause / set-price / resume-sale work frozen (the design record D2 order)")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
(env-keys ["admin-key"])
(expect "pause works frozen" "sale paused" (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.pause))
(expect "is-active reflects the frozen pause" false (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.is-active))
;; the design record D2 sequence: the reprice happens while PAUSED — the only state where it is
;; legal at all — then the sale reopens. Both the operation AND the lockout must
;; survive the freeze: an enforce that stopped enforcing frozen would be a defect the
;; same way an operation that stopped working would.
(expect "set-price works frozen (while paused)" "price updated" (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.set-price 0.75))
(expect "the frozen price update took" 0.75 (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.get-price))
(expect "resume-sale works frozen" "sale resumed" (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.resume-sale))
(expect-failure "D2 lockout still enforced frozen: set-price refused while active"
  "SPT price is locked while the sale is active"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.set-price 0.8))
(expect "the refused frozen reprice changed nothing" 0.75 (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.get-price))
(commit-tx)

(begin-tx "3 the design record part 2: BOTH SETTABLE LIMITS STILL MOVE FROZEN, and their floors still hold")
;; 🔴 THIS IS THE AUDIT #7 a finding SHAPE, AND IT IS THE WHOLE POINT OF the design record PART 2.
;; a finding was an operation that needed authority which DIED at freeze: the gas station's `init`
;; composed `GOVERNANCE`, which enforces `(not FROZEN-MODULE)`, so a frozen station could never
;; be created on a new chain. A settable limit whose SETTER stopped working at freeze would be
;; the same defect and a worse one — the design record's Consequences say in terms that "after freeze, a
;; settable limit stays settable forever". A limit that freezes at whatever value it happened to
;; hold is just a defconst with extra steps, and the founder's whole reason for asking was that
;; today's number may be wrong later.
;; So: both setters take ADMIN-GOV, NOT GOVERNANCE. This asserts that difference instead of
;; trusting it — swap either to GOVERNANCE and these four lines go red.
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
(env-keys ["admin-key"])
(expect "set-runway works frozen" "runway updated"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.set-runway 86400))
(expect "the frozen runway change took" 86400
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-runway))
;; and the HARD MINIMUM is still enforced frozen — a floor that stopped holding at freeze
;; would be strictly worse than one that never existed, because the docs would still claim it.
(expect-failure "the runway floor STILL refuses frozen"
  "SPT runway must be at least"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.set-runway 60))
(expect "the refused frozen runway change moved nothing" 86400
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-runway))
;; The sale must be CLOSED to move the price floor, so pause around it — the same the design record D2
;; sequence set-price uses, and it must survive the freeze too.
(n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.pause)
(expect "set-min-price works frozen" "price floor updated"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.set-min-price 0.005))
(expect "the frozen price-floor change took" 0.005
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.get-min-price))
(expect-failure "the price floor's HARD minimum still refuses frozen"
  "SPT price floor must be at least"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.set-min-price 0.0000001))
(expect "the refused frozen floor change moved nothing" 0.005
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.get-min-price))
(n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.resume-sale)
;; Rolled back: this block moves two limits, and every later assertion in this file was written
;; against the seeded values.
(rollback-tx)

(begin-tx "3 launch withdraw-proceeds works frozen — the KDA exit survives")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
;; a later change (founder ): WITHDRAW-PROCEEDS is @managed on amount, so an unscoped
;; signature cannot drive it. The clist names the capability with the SAME destination and
;; amount the call spends — and it must keep working on a FROZEN module.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "admin-key"
        , "caps": [(n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.WITHDRAW-PROCEEDS "sender00" 100.0)] }])
(expect "withdraw-proceeds works frozen" "proceeds withdrawn"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.withdraw-proceeds "sender00" 100.0))
(commit-tx)

;; ===========================================================================
;; §4 — THE OTHER HALF OF THE INVARIANT: THE UPGRADE PATH IS STILL REFUSED.
;;
;; 🔴 WITHOUT IT EVERYTHING ABOVE IS SATISFIED BY A MODULE THAT SIMPLY IS NOT FROZEN. A change
;; that made every operation work by weakening the freeze itself would be catastrophic AND
;; would look green.
;;
;; IT CANNOT LIVE IN THIS FILE, and the reason is a trap this repo has already paid for: a
;; module `load` that fails is a COMPILE-TIME abort which leaves the parser inside the
;; module's namespace, so `expect-failure` cannot catch it (measured here: wrapping the
;; redeploy produced "Cannot find module: rollback-tx" — the suite died rather than asserting).
;; That is exactly why every other unresolvable-load claim in this repo is a `.repl-must-fail`
;; fixture asserted from OUTSIDE on the exit code AND the error text.
;;
;; So the two halves live in:
;; pact/test/frozen-upgrade-tokens.repl-must-fail
;; pact/test/frozen-upgrade-launch.repl-must-fail
;; both registered in run-tests.sh's MUSTFAIL map against "Module is frozen".
;; ===========================================================================

;; ===========================================================================
;; §5 — THE NOT-RUNNABLE FUNCTIONS, PROVEN NOT-RUNNABLE FOR A NON-FREEZE REASON.
;; This is what turns "could not run it" from an excuse into evidence: each refusal is the
;; function's OWN precondition, and none of them is "Module is frozen".
;; ===========================================================================
(begin-tx "5 init-supply refuses for its ONE-SHOT guard, not the freeze")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
(env-data { "spt-gov": { "keys": ["admin-key"], "pred": "keys-all" } })
(env-keys ["admin-key"])
(expect-failure "init-supply: already initialized, NOT frozen"
  "module already initialized"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.init-supply
    (read-keyset 'spt-gov)
    [ { "account": "kf", "amount": 1.0 } ]))
(rollback-tx)

(begin-tx "5 init refuses for its CHAIN guard, not the freeze")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
(env-keys ["admin-key"])
(expect-failure "tokens.init: chain-0 guard, NOT frozen"
  "Use init-supply on chain 0"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.init
    n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.LAUNCH-RESERVE-G))   ; the design record D3 4th arg — arity only; the chain guard fires first
(rollback-tx)

(begin-tx "5 launch.init refuses for its ONE-SHOT guard, not the freeze")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
(env-keys ["admin-key"])
(expect-failure "launch.init: already initialized, NOT frozen"
  "sale already initialized"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT-launch.init 0.5))
(rollback-tx)

;; ===========================================================================
;; §6 — the design record (a later change): THE SIXTEEN NEW FUNCTIONS, EVERY ONE DISPOSITIONED.
;;
;; 🔴 THREE OF THESE ARE THE AUDIT #7 a finding SHAPE AND ARE EXERCISED FOR THAT REASON.
;; `schedule-snapshot` and `cancel-snapshot` are ADMIN-gated and `advance-snapshot` WRITES.
;; a finding was exactly this: the gas station's `init` composed `GOVERNANCE`, whose body enforces
;; `(not FROZEN-MODULE)`, so a frozen station could never be created — an operation that died
;; at the freeze, permanently, because a frozen module cannot be upgraded to repair it.
;; If any of these three died the same way, a frozen chain could never seal another record
;; date, and since the design record makes a sealed record date a PRECONDITION of `declare-round`, the
;; ENTIRE award subsystem would be dead on that chain forever. That is not something to
;; assume from reading the caps — it is asserted here against a module compiled frozen.
;; (`ADMIN` gates on the admin keyset and never touches FROZEN-MODULE; the point is to prove
;; it, because a finding reached an the reviewer precisely because no test could fail.)
;; ===========================================================================
(begin-tx "6 the design record reads all answer on a FROZEN module")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
;; RELATIONAL, not a magic number: §2 sealed a generation on this frozen chain, so the
;; assertion is that the readers AGREE with each other and with the row — which is what an
;; operator sweeping 20 frozen chains actually depends on.
(expect "get-snapshot-gen: a generation HAS sealed on this frozen chain" true
  (>= (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-snapshot-gen) 1))
(expect "get-snapshot: the live generation reads back exists:true, frozen" true
  (at 'exists (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-snapshot (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-snapshot-gen))))
(expect "get-snapshot-at: EPOCH means none scheduled" true
  (= (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-snapshot-at)
     n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.EPOCH))
;; get-total-distributed exists BECAUSE its absence was a freeze defect: `total-distributed`
;; was the one state field with no getter at all, and after the freeze it is unreachable.
;; Two independent readers of the same field must agree — the getter exists BECAUSE
;; `total-distributed` was otherwise unreachable after the freeze.
(expect "get-total-distributed: agrees with chain-report, frozen"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-total-distributed)
  (at 'total-distributed (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.chain-report)))
(expect "snapshot-circulating: IS the sealed row's circ, frozen"
  (at 'circ (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-snapshot (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-snapshot-gen)))
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.snapshot-circulating))
;; get-snapshot NEVER aborts on a missing generation — the `exists` idiom, so a 20-chain
;; comparator can sweep every generation on every chain in one pass on a FROZEN module.
(expect "get-snapshot: a never-sealed generation reports exists:false, frozen"
  { "gen": 999, "exists": false, "circ": 0.0, "base": 0.0, "rate": 0.0 }
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-snapshot 999))
(expect "get-snapshot: generation 0 and below are out of range, not an abort" false
  (at 'exists (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-snapshot 0)))
(expect "gkey: the generation key helper" "7"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.gkey 7))
(commit-tx)

(begin-tx "6 the correction arithmetic is pure and answers frozen")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
;; idx 0 reads no snapshot row, so both are total functions on a chain that never sealed.
(expect "snap-m: a never-checkpointed row measures against rpt itself" 0.25
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.snap-m 0 0.25))
(expect "snap-corr-of: a never-checkpointed row has NO correction" 0.0
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.snap-corr-of 0 0.0 100.0 0.0 0.25))
(expect "snap-open: nothing sealed, so nothing is unfolded" 0.0
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.snap-open 0.25))
;; A generation IS open here, so a never-checkpointed row's checkpoint DOES fire — it
;; freezes the pre-operation balance into the live generation. `corr` is still 0.0 (idx 0
;; carries no correction), which is the half that matters for the arithmetic.
(expect "plan-snap: an unchecked row has no correction to crystallize, frozen" 0.0
  (at 'corr (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.plan-snap 0 0.0 100.0 90.0 0.0 0.0)))
(expect "plan-snap: and it checkpoints into the LIVE generation, frozen"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-snapshot-gen)
  (at 'index (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.plan-snap 0 0.0 100.0 90.0 0.0 0.0)))
(commit-tx)

(begin-tx "6 the operator reads answer frozen — chain-report is the founder's one call")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
;; The bar and the tool that reports it must agree — one implementation, two callers.
(expect "round-funding-bar: IS what funding-needed reports, frozen"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.round-funding-bar 0.01)
  (at 'required (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.funding-needed 0.01)))
(expect "funding-needed: a shortfall is never negative, frozen" true
  (>= (at 'shortfall (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.funding-needed 0.01)) 0.0))
;; chain-report wraps its reserve reads in `try` precisely so it answers on the nineteen
;; SPOKES, where the launch reserve row does not exist. A frozen spoke is where an operator
;; needs it most, and an aborting read there would be unfixable.
(expect "chain-report: answers in one call on a frozen module, and agrees"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.get-snapshot-gen)
  (at 'generation (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.chain-report)))
(commit-tx)

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; 🔴 THE THREE THAT WRITE. If these die at freeze the award subsystem dies with them.
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(begin-tx "6 advance-snapshot: PERMISSIONLESS and WRITES, and it still runs frozen")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
(env-keys [])                       ; no keys at all — it must not need any
(expect "advance-snapshot: no-ops cleanly on a frozen module, unsigned" "no-seal"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.advance-snapshot))
(commit-tx)

(begin-tx "6 schedule-snapshot: ADMIN-gated, and the freeze does NOT revoke it")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
(env-keys ["admin-key"])
(expect "schedule-snapshot: a record date can still be named on a FROZEN module"
  "record date scheduled"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.schedule-snapshot
    (time "2026-06-13T00:00:00Z")))
;; ...and the only way back is still open too. Both or neither: a schedulable-but-not-
;; cancellable record date on a frozen module would be a permanent mis-dating.
(expect "cancel-snapshot: and it is still cancellable on a FROZEN module"
  "record date cancelled"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.cancel-snapshot))
(rollback-tx)

(begin-tx "6 and the ADMIN gate is still a real gate on a frozen module")
(env-chain-data { "chain-id": "0", "block-time": (time "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z") })
(env-keys [])
;; Surviving the freeze must not mean becoming permissionless — the negative is the other
;; half of the claim, and without it "it still runs frozen" could be true for a stranger too.
(expect-failure "schedule-snapshot: a stranger is still refused, frozen"
  "Keyset failure"
  (n_48867b242317a0216a67f8c7ca26696b5878e0e3.SPT.schedule-snapshot
    (time "2026-06-13T00:00:00Z")))
(rollback-tx)

;; 🔴 THE BANNER NAMES ITS OWN LIMIT (a later change / `L4-03`). It used to read "every enumerated
;; function survives the freeze", full stop — which an operator reads as a freeze clearance, and
;; which was false: §1a measures a real outage in the window between freezing the token and
;; re-deploying the sale. Every claim below is scoped to what this file actually executes.
(print "smartpacts-frozen-invariant suite PASSED — every enumerated function survives the freeze ONCE THE SALE IS RE-LINKED (§1a measures the outage before it; the bless rescue that removes the window is node-measured by bless-drill.ts D1/D2, a later change); upgrade still refused on both modules. NOT a freeze clearance — the operator runbook gates the operator runbook.")
